    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (74.91) and **Lawrence Butler** (71.64) anchor our attack as the clear top-tier plays. **Bryce Harper** draws a prime matchup against Eric Lauer, whose 5.41 xERA provides a massive boost to our anchor\u2019s base projection; with the favorable park factor and a spot in the #3 hole, he is an auto-start for both power and reliability. **Lawrence Butler** is our most intriguing high-upside play, benefiting significantly from an elite 19% boost in SP skill against Merrill Kelly. Despite hitting lower in the order, his 13% platoon edge makes him a high-efficiency engine for production today. **Taylor Ward** (68.65) rounds out our elite tier, taking advantage of a strong platoon matchup against Bennett to solidify the top of the lineup.\n\nOur optimizer prioritized efficiency and platoon advantages, which led to the omission of **Drew Gilbert** (50.48), our closest bench decision. While **Drew Gilbert** benefited from the same park and skill factors as **Luis Arraez**, his projected role at the bottom of the order and our league-wide scarcity of speed relative to the efficiency provided by starters like **Jonathan Aranda** (63.20) kept him on the pine. **Jonathan Aranda** was ultimately given the nod for the UTIL slot due to a superior 12% dynamic platoon edge, which provides a higher probability of daily contribution than the raw upside of **Drew Gilbert**.\n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, as a shift for **Gleyber Torres** or **Geraldo Perdomo** could swing their daily efficiency scores. **Gleyber Torres** in particular is carrying a slight risk with a reported \"Wind In\" factor (-5%) dampening his raw output against Colin Rea. We are comfortable with our current configuration, but we remain vigilant regarding weather risks for our bench; specifically, **Gavin Sheets** is being held out of the lineup not just due to the optimizer\u2019s preference for others, but also because of a 35% rain risk that further diminishes his value. **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** remain solid, if unspectacular, starts as we look to capitalize on soft spots in the opposing rotations of Singer and Alcantara.",
